ReversePort adaptation
======================

Two fathom components adapt methods from ReversePort
(laaielichter/ReversePort, MIT License, (c) laaielichter and
contributors), specifically its `port/` layer:

- `infer_struct` (crates/fathom-native/src/structinfer.rs): the
  sample-comparison format inference of ReversePort's `re_struct`
  tool — constant runs with the big-endian give-back, length /
  count / checksum / time / offset relations, record-table column
  typing, trailer digests, and the Kaitai draft shape.
- The injection shield (crates/fathom-core/src/shield.rs, wired
  into the MCP result path in crates/fathom-mcp/src/server.rs):
  the rule kinds, budgets, and `untrusted`-note semantics of
  ReversePort's injection shield for tool results.

The Rust implementations are estate-authored from the published
specs and behavioral tests; no JavaScript source was copied into
the tree. ReversePort's REA-derived deep-analysis engine was not
used in any way.
